{
 "method": "forecast_v2 (pre-registered backtest winner). grain = latest pre-January NASS grain-area forecast (Nov 14 2025; Sep 12 2025 where November omits the state) as is (NASS: latest pre-January NASS grain forecast as is). silage = R2, MED5: (D' + PERSIST) / 2, D' shares = 5-year medians: the average of method D with 5-year median shares (2020-2024) and last year's silage acres. Selection: ROUND 2 (run after round 1's 2025 score was seen): lowest 2018-2024 acre-weighted absolute % error among R1-R3, replacing S5 only if >= 0.50 pp better and median APE not > 0.50 pp worse; pre-registered in forecast_v2/PREREGISTRATION.md \"Round 2\"; 2025 answers never used to fit or choose. SE = estimate x the backtest RMS relative error of its size class; 95% range = estimate +/- z SE with z the 95th percentile of backtest |error|/SE; covered_by_95_interval is leave-one-year-out. US: SE = estimate x RMS of the backtest US relative errors, 95% range = +/- t(0.975, n-1) SE. Each convergence date is re-estimated with only what was known then and gets its own range, calibrated on the backtest errors of that release.",
 "answer_key_excluded": "Crop Production Annual Summary, January 2026 (cropan26), the judges' file and every 2025 YEAR value are never read; the planted export's 2025 YEAR rows were removed before commit.",
